# ── secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# And never a copy: a `.env.bak` was once committed to the repository this was
# split out of, and every key in it had to be rotated. The glob is wide for that
# reason, and `!.env.example` is the only way back in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pem

# ── build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every one of these is regenerated by `pnpm build`, and several of them bake in
# the API origin, so a tracked copy is both noise and a small leak.
dist/
dist-*/
build/
staging/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/

# ── packaged applications ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
apps/mobile/dist/
apps/tizen/dist/
apps/webos/dist/
*.apk
*.aab
*.wgt
*.ipk

# Except the Samsung store artwork, which is an INPUT to a submission rather
# than build output — whoever does the upload should not have to regenerate it.
!apps/tizen/store/

# ── android ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
apps/mobile/android/.gradle/
apps/mobile/android/app/build/
apps/mobile/android/build/
apps/mobile/android/local.properties
apps/mobile/android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/

# ── ios ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The project itself is committed; what Xcode, CocoaPods and the CLI generate is not.
apps/mobile/ios/App/Pods/
apps/mobile/ios/App/build/
apps/mobile/ios/App/output/
apps/mobile/ios/App/App/public/
apps/mobile/ios/App/App/capacitor.config.json
apps/mobile/ios/App/App/config.xml
apps/mobile/ios/DerivedData/
apps/mobile/ios/capacitor-cordova-ios-plugins/
apps/mobile/ios/**/xcuserdata/
*.xcarchive
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.mobileprovision

# ── dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# ── editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── logs and scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
tmp/

# ── development tooling: kept on disk, kept out of the repository ─────────────
# The browser probes and one-off sweeps are how behaviour gets verified here —
# they drive a real browser and assert on what is on screen — but they are a
# working tool, not part of the product, and several of them carry fixtures and
# subject matter that has no business in a handover. They stay in the working
# directory and out of git.
#
# What deliberately REMAINS tracked, because a clean checkout has to build and
# test itself without them: the build and release chain (stamp-build, css-compat,
# version, brand-*, release-notes, publish, announce, android-env, dev/api/stop),
# the gates that run in `pnpm test` (*.test.mjs), scripts/lib, conformance,
# bundle-floor, fake-panel and store-shots.
scripts/*-probe.mjs
scripts/*-sweep.mjs
scripts/scroll-stress.mjs
scripts/section-sweep.mjs
scripts/route-sweep.mjs
scripts/style-audit.mjs
scripts/brand-check.mjs
scripts/tv-shot.mjs
scripts/tv-emulator.sh
scripts/wrapper-check.sh

# ── large data and source material: kept on disk, kept out of git ────────────
# `catalogue.json` is a 2.2MB snapshot of a real provider's listing. Nothing in
# the test suite loads it — every reference to it in the code is a COMMENT
# citing a measurement taken from it — so tracking it bought nothing and cost
# more than the rest of the repository put together. `scripts/conformance.mts`
# and `scripts/fake-panel.mjs` read it; both are development tools. Regenerate
# or ask for a copy; `fixtures/README.md` says how.
fixtures/catalogue.json

# Raw brand source material — the originals a logo was cut from, including
# photographs sent over WhatsApp. What the app SHIPS is generated into
# `apps/web/public`, so none of this is needed to build.
#
# Except `logo.png`, which is: `brand.config.json` names it, `brandRev` in
# scripts/brand-kit.mjs hashes it to version the splash artwork, and
# scripts/brand-rev.test.mjs fails without it. Found by cloning the repository
# into an empty directory and running the suite — a grep for "brand/" missed it
# because the path is built from the config rather than written down.
brand/*
!brand/logo.png

# Store screenshots for the Samsung submission. Regenerated by
# `scripts/store-shots.mjs`, and every one of them is full of a third party's
# poster artwork, which is not ours to redistribute. The three brand images
# beside them (logo, background, icon) ARE ours and stay.
apps/tizen/store/screenshot-*.jpg

# The remuxer's own wasm, copied out of node_modules at build time —
# a copy of the vendored libav.js build, made at build time. See apps/web/scripts/libav-assets.mjs.
apps/web/public/libav/

.work/
.tv-vnc-pass
.work-shots/
